1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000

3
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:46,041
Neil!

4
00:00:47,166 --> 00:00:48,458
Neil!

5
00:00:52,166 --> 00:00:53,458
Neil Spencer!

6
00:00:53,958 --> 00:00:55,666
Neil Spencer!

7
00:00:57,916 --> 00:00:59,083
Neil!

8
00:00:59,916 --> 00:01:02,082
Anything more on the parents?

9
00:01:02,083 --> 00:01:04,207
<i>Background checks dug up nothing new.</i>

10
00:01:04,208 --> 00:01:08,458
<i>Dad's AWOL, mom's in rehab,
grandma's been taking care of the boy.</i>

11
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:09,916
All right.

12
00:01:10,416 --> 00:01:12,623
I want all interviews
with immediate family in the area

13
00:01:12,624 --> 00:01:13,915
complete by the end of the day.

14
00:01:13,916 --> 00:01:15,166
<i>Yes, Detective.</i>

15
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:17,374
Neil!

16
00:01:17,999 --> 00:01:20,165
- Neil!
- <i>This is not a race.</i>

17
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:22,498
<i>Take your time.
We're looking for a missing child.</i>

18
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,083
All right, people.

19
00:01:24,624 --> 00:01:25,623
Listen up!

20
00:01:25,624 --> 00:01:28,873
All right, Neil Spencer was put to bed
around 8:00 p.m. last night.

21
00:01:28,874 --> 00:01:32,957
His grandmother reported him missing
at 10:29 p.m.

22
00:01:32,958 --> 00:01:36,123
Be prepared to call your families
and let them know you won't be home.

23
00:01:36,124 --> 00:01:38,666
Detective! We found something.

24
00:02:08,916 --> 00:02:10,708
This isn't Neil Spencer.

25
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:36,832
<i>Meet me in the crowd...</i>

26
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:39,666
You know, I'm excited.
It's a fresh start, right?

27
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:42,790
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

28
00:02:42,791 --> 00:02:46,249
You know, your mom always wanted us
to move back to the town we grew up in.

29
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:49,957
You know, it's cool. You'll be going
to the same school she did. Right?

30
00:02:49,958 --> 00:02:51,166
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

31
00:02:52,166 --> 00:02:54,373
Plus, we found a house with a swing.

32
00:02:54,374 --> 00:02:57,707
I mean, it's just like the one
you guys loved at the shore.

33
00:02:57,708 --> 00:02:59,540
You've said.

34
00:02:59,541 --> 00:03:01,123
Like a thousand times.

35
00:03:01,124 --> 00:03:02,790
No, no, no. No, that's incorrect.

36
00:03:02,791 --> 00:03:04,957
I've only said it 936 times.

37
00:03:04,958 --> 00:03:06,916
So get your facts straight.

38
00:03:11,791 --> 00:03:13,083
I miss her.

39
00:03:15,999 --> 00:03:17,166
Me too, buddy.

40
00:03:19,874 --> 00:03:22,999
Up! Get your legs up.
Get 'em up. Come on. Up, up, up, up, up!

41
00:03:24,291 --> 00:03:27,498
And... we are in Garretton.

42
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:29,290
<i>Everyone around...</i>

43
00:03:29,291 --> 00:03:30,249
We did it.

44
00:03:30,958 --> 00:03:34,957
<i>Love them, love them</i>

45
00:03:34,958 --> 00:03:38,540
<i>Put it in your hands</i>

46
00:03:38,541 --> 00:03:42,291
<i>Take it, take it...</i>

47
00:03:59,291 --> 00:04:00,416
There it is.

48
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:03,290
- Wanna go check it out?
- Yeah.

49
00:04:03,291 --> 00:04:04,166
Go ahead.

50
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:07,040
- Hey, guys.
- What's up?

51
00:04:07,041 --> 00:04:10,207
Hey, how you doing?
Uh, where do you want these, sir?

52
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:13,249
Yeah, you know what?
Those can go in the kitchen. Thank you.

53
00:04:19,499 --> 00:04:22,458
- Hey, Dad! Look at this!
- Be right there, buddy.

54
00:04:32,166 --> 00:04:34,666
I hope this place is
big enough for you, Jake.

55
00:04:48,624 --> 00:04:51,790
All right, come on, kiddo.
We got a new house, new stairs.

56
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:53,333
What did we say we were gonna be?

57
00:04:55,791 --> 00:04:56,916
Brave.

58
00:04:57,416 --> 00:04:58,541
That's right.

59
00:04:59,166 --> 00:05:01,458
Just like your mom when she was sick.

60
00:05:03,624 --> 00:05:04,458
Come here.

61
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:09,416
All right. Let's go upstairs.

62
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,166
Yeah.

63
00:05:15,249 --> 00:05:17,208
And...

64
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:19,166
Go find your room.

65
00:05:49,708 --> 00:05:50,916
What's wrong?

66
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:54,083
Why are you so scared?

67
00:05:57,249 --> 00:05:58,541
It's gonna be fine.

68
00:06:02,666 --> 00:06:05,248
No, not... No! Wait a second.

69
00:06:05,249 --> 00:06:06,457
You can't take him.

70
00:06:06,458 --> 00:06:08,082
Okay, Saturn's going...

71
00:06:08,083 --> 00:06:10,207
Do-do-do-do-do-do!

72
00:06:10,208 --> 00:06:11,207
...right up to the sun.

73
00:06:11,208 --> 00:06:12,207
Do-do-do-do!

74
00:06:12,208 --> 00:06:13,790
- No!
- Chain reaction.

75
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:14,707
No!

76
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:16,416
Oh no!

77
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:21,165
All right. Uh...

78
00:06:21,166 --> 00:06:22,832
- Okay. You ready?
- Yeah.

79
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:24,833
Good? It's gonna be great. Okay?

80
00:06:26,124 --> 00:06:29,249
You warm enough?
Yeah? Wanna hang onto that?

81
00:06:29,999 --> 00:06:30,833
You sure?

82
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:32,998
Yeah?

83
00:06:32,999 --> 00:06:34,123
Okay. All right.

84
00:06:34,124 --> 00:06:35,166
Come here.

85
00:06:36,208 --> 00:06:38,373
All right. Have a good day, okay?

86
00:06:38,374 --> 00:06:40,708
I'm gonna be right here
when school gets out, all right?

87
00:06:41,208 --> 00:06:43,458
- Okay. Okay?
- Hmm.

88
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:34,249
Oh fuck.

89
00:07:41,249 --> 00:07:42,583
Jesus.

90
00:08:18,624 --> 00:08:21,166
<i>If your window's left unlatched</i>

91
00:08:21,999 --> 00:08:24,458
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

92
00:09:54,666 --> 00:09:56,666
<i>What kind of fish were they?</i>

93
00:09:57,166 --> 00:09:58,707
<i>I don't know.</i>

94
00:09:58,708 --> 00:10:02,124
<i>There was a pink one. And a blue one.</i>

95
00:10:03,041 --> 00:10:04,999
<i>Do you think they'll miss you?</i>

96
00:10:05,791 --> 00:10:07,373
<i>My fish?</i>

97
00:10:07,374 --> 00:10:10,624
<i>You fed them, right?
Like your daddy fed you.</i>

98
00:10:11,124 --> 00:10:14,374
<i>Do you think they'll miss you
feeding them?</i>

99
00:10:15,708 --> 00:10:18,291
- <i>I don't know.</i>
- <i>Speak up, boy.</i>

100
00:10:18,874 --> 00:10:21,124
<i>What if they get hungry
and you're not there?</i>

101
00:10:21,624 --> 00:10:23,583
<i>Do you think they'll eat each other?</i>

102
00:10:24,333 --> 00:10:28,624
<i>When one fish is shitting out the other,
will they be thinking of you?</i>

103
00:10:37,541 --> 00:10:38,708
Good.

104
00:10:39,999 --> 00:10:42,499
Good. I think they're going to love this.

105
00:10:47,124 --> 00:10:48,541
That's for later.

106
00:11:29,874 --> 00:11:31,249
Hi, Mr. Willis.

107
00:11:31,749 --> 00:11:34,124
Uh, Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

108
00:11:34,624 --> 00:11:35,583
May I come in?

109
00:11:36,749 --> 00:11:38,499
I'm sorry to interrupt your dinner.

110
00:11:39,124 --> 00:11:42,373
Uh, a boy went missing
in Hillcrest a couple of days ago.

111
00:11:42,374 --> 00:11:43,707
Neil Spencer.

112
00:11:43,708 --> 00:11:46,249
We've cleared locations,
family, and friends.

113
00:11:46,874 --> 00:11:50,624
We found something, and I don't know
if it's a lead or a distraction.

114
00:11:54,666 --> 00:11:56,623
Another body. A boy.

115
00:11:56,624 --> 00:11:58,541
Been out in the woods about a month.

116
00:12:04,749 --> 00:12:06,873
Not every kid
who disappears in North Jersey

117
00:12:06,874 --> 00:12:08,873
is connected to Frank Carter, Detective.

118
00:12:08,874 --> 00:12:10,832
But that's his signature, right?

119
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:13,374
Well, Frank Carter's doing life
in Rahway now.

120
00:12:14,291 --> 00:12:15,416
That's not what I asked.

121
00:12:17,124 --> 00:12:20,998
I know you need to find him, of course,
but I don't know if I can help you.

122
00:12:20,999 --> 00:12:23,123
The other boy who went missing,
Neil Spencer,

123
00:12:23,124 --> 00:12:26,916
told his grandma he heard a strange voice
outside his window

124
00:12:27,749 --> 00:12:29,041
whispering to him.

125
00:12:31,708 --> 00:12:34,457
Well, you know,
kids have active imaginations--

126
00:12:34,458 --> 00:12:37,123
Yes, that's what Carter preyed on.
That's what you said.

127
00:12:37,124 --> 00:12:39,290
I did, but, you know,
I'm not on the job anymore.

128
00:12:39,291 --> 00:12:42,165
It's been a long time.
I'm retired at least 25 years.

129
00:12:42,166 --> 00:12:44,457
I just, you know...
And there's only one Frank Carter.

130
00:12:44,458 --> 00:12:48,915
Your case file mentioned an accomplice
to Carter who was never identified.

131
00:12:48,916 --> 00:12:51,498
I did. I did.
It was a theory, and it went cold.

132
00:12:51,499 --> 00:12:52,499
They often do.

133
00:12:59,874 --> 00:13:03,040
Frank Carter still declines all interviews
via his lawyers.

134
00:13:03,041 --> 00:13:05,582
You remain the only one
he's ever agreed to speak with

135
00:13:05,583 --> 00:13:08,541
since his, uh, incarceration.

136
00:13:09,666 --> 00:13:11,540
Got any advice interviewing him?

137
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:13,333
Yeah, I'd say don't.

138
00:13:16,124 --> 00:13:18,083
I... I hope you find your kid.

139
00:13:18,583 --> 00:13:21,458
With all due respect, sir,
hope does nothing for me.

140
00:13:57,749 --> 00:14:00,790
Can I put this
in my Packet of Special Things?

141
00:14:00,791 --> 00:14:02,208
Let me see.

142
00:14:07,708 --> 00:14:08,541
Sure.

143
00:14:15,416 --> 00:14:16,624
What's that?

144
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:19,957
We made our hands be in paint
on the wall at school.

145
00:14:19,958 --> 00:14:21,748
Oh, yeah? Handprints, huh?

146
00:14:21,749 --> 00:14:23,207
- Mm-hmm.
- Cool.

147
00:14:23,208 --> 00:14:24,583
My friend helped me.

148
00:14:26,374 --> 00:14:28,416
Oh, yeah? You make a friend?

149
00:14:29,416 --> 00:14:31,124
The girl in the blue sweater.

150
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:36,123
Well, do you remember
we talked about that?

151
00:14:36,124 --> 00:14:38,499
How some friends are pretend and...

152
00:14:42,541 --> 00:14:43,708
What's up, bud?

153
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:48,123
Are you sure she won't wake up?

154
00:14:48,124 --> 00:14:49,083
Mommy?

155
00:14:50,499 --> 00:14:51,624
I am.

156
00:14:54,041 --> 00:14:56,374
You know, Mommy loved you

157
00:14:57,541 --> 00:15:01,708
more than anything, you know,
and that's... that's never gonna change.

158
00:15:02,249 --> 00:15:06,415
But it doesn't mean
that you can't make room for new people,

159
00:15:06,416 --> 00:15:08,708
you know, new... new friends.

160
00:15:09,374 --> 00:15:11,916
I don't like the boys at school.

161
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:16,083
You know,

162
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:18,540
I never told you this,

163
00:15:18,541 --> 00:15:23,582
but when I was your age,
I had a friend, just like you have.

164
00:15:23,583 --> 00:15:24,582
I did.

165
00:15:24,583 --> 00:15:27,749
He'd visit me when I was going to sleep,
and we'd go on adventures.

166
00:15:28,416 --> 00:15:30,040
At the end, every time,

167
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:32,540
he would kiss me on the forehead,
right here.

168
00:15:32,541 --> 00:15:33,624
And then

169
00:15:34,499 --> 00:15:38,458
I'd wake up the next morning
back in bed like magic.

170
00:15:39,083 --> 00:15:41,458
I called him Mr. Night.

171
00:15:43,416 --> 00:15:46,373
It's okay to imagine things, Jake.

172
00:15:46,374 --> 00:15:48,124
You just... You gotta

173
00:15:49,041 --> 00:15:51,666
give real people a chance, too, okay?

174
00:16:18,041 --> 00:16:19,624
What is your name?

175
00:16:25,916 --> 00:16:27,166
It's okay.

176
00:16:28,291 --> 00:16:29,999
They need to hear this.

177
00:17:26,791 --> 00:17:29,457
Hey! Sorry! Sorry, I'm late.

178
00:17:29,458 --> 00:17:32,416
- You're Jake's father?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Hi. How you doing?

179
00:17:33,208 --> 00:17:34,665
Buddy, what's wrong?

180
00:17:34,666 --> 00:17:36,833
You wanna tell your dad what happened?

181
00:17:37,624 --> 00:17:39,415
I got put on yellow.

182
00:17:39,416 --> 00:17:40,790
You... On what?

183
00:17:40,791 --> 00:17:43,291
We have a traffic light system
for bad behavior.

184
00:17:43,874 --> 00:17:45,999
What'd he do? Uh, what'd you do?

185
00:17:46,583 --> 00:17:49,290
Owen tried to take
my Packet of Special Things.

186
00:17:49,291 --> 00:17:51,748
He scratched a boy. Badly.

187
00:17:51,749 --> 00:17:55,040
Okay, well, that's...
You can't do that, Jake.

188
00:17:55,041 --> 00:17:57,582
Um, sorry. It's this packet.

189
00:17:57,583 --> 00:18:01,290
Um, it's full of stuff that,
like, belonged to his mom.

190
00:18:01,291 --> 00:18:02,749
That's no excuse.

191
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:06,583
We'd like him to write a note apologizing.

192
00:18:07,916 --> 00:18:09,832
Uh, isn't that excessive?

193
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:12,415
We have zero tolerance
for kids hurting kids.

194
00:18:12,416 --> 00:18:14,040
What's your tolerance for bullies?

195
00:18:14,041 --> 00:18:16,582
'Cause that other kid
sounds like kind of a dick.

196
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:19,582
- Excuse me?
- You know what? We'll pass on that note.

197
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:20,499
Come on, buddy.

198
00:18:21,666 --> 00:18:23,249
You can put me on yellow.

199
00:18:29,791 --> 00:18:30,749
Where is it?

200
00:18:35,749 --> 00:18:38,915
<i>I didn't like being there,</i>

201
00:18:38,916 --> 00:18:40,541
<i>that house.</i>

202
00:18:41,083 --> 00:18:42,791
<i>Your grandmother's.</i>

203
00:18:43,666 --> 00:18:45,791
<i>Was she mean to you</i>?

204
00:18:46,833 --> 00:18:49,291
<i>No. Sometimes</i>

205
00:18:49,916 --> 00:18:51,541
<i>she was sick.</i>

206
00:18:52,958 --> 00:18:54,458
<i>I was afraid.</i>

207
00:18:55,083 --> 00:18:56,499
<i>It's okay.</i>

208
00:18:57,291 --> 00:18:59,124
<i>They need to hear it.</i>

209
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:03,248
<i>I was afraid she'd die.</i>

210
00:19:03,249 --> 00:19:07,041
<i>She'd be dead in the house with me
while I slept.</i>

211
00:19:08,291 --> 00:19:11,416
<i>If you could talk to your mommy right now,</i>

212
00:19:12,333 --> 00:19:13,749
<i>what would you say?</i>

213
00:19:16,041 --> 00:19:18,166
<i>Why did you leave me there?</i>

214
00:19:18,874 --> 00:19:20,666
<i>Why don't you love me?</i>

215
00:19:22,291 --> 00:19:23,708
<i>I love you.</i>

216
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:30,333
<i>Free your mind And the rest will follow</i>

217
00:19:30,874 --> 00:19:33,332
<i>Be color blind</i>

218
00:19:33,333 --> 00:19:34,999
<i>Don't be so shallow</i>

219
00:19:35,958 --> 00:19:39,999
<i>Free your mind
And the rest will follow</i>

220
00:20:51,249 --> 00:20:54,207
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

221
00:20:54,208 --> 00:20:56,833
<i>Soon you'll hear the whispers spoken</i>

222
00:20:57,541 --> 00:20:59,790
<i>If your window is left unlatched</i>

223
00:20:59,791 --> 00:21:02,249
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

224
00:21:03,291 --> 00:21:04,333
Jake?

225
00:21:05,708 --> 00:21:06,916
What are you doing?

226
00:21:11,666 --> 00:21:12,583
Jake!

227
00:21:13,583 --> 00:21:14,708
No!

228
00:21:27,708 --> 00:21:29,082
Who were you talking to?

229
00:21:29,083 --> 00:21:30,416
Nobody.

230
00:21:45,374 --> 00:21:46,291
Back to bed.

231
00:22:46,791 --> 00:22:47,833
Hey!

232
00:22:50,874 --> 00:22:53,248
Hey! What are you doing?

233
00:22:53,249 --> 00:22:55,583
Hey! Hey! Hey!

234
00:23:02,041 --> 00:23:05,957
We've had reports of a squatter
since the place went vacant.

235
00:23:05,958 --> 00:23:10,123
Kids sneaking in to drink
and do other things.

236
00:23:10,124 --> 00:23:11,708
This wasn't a kid.

237
00:23:14,208 --> 00:23:15,083
What's back here?

238
00:23:16,666 --> 00:23:17,791
I don't know.

239
00:23:24,208 --> 00:23:26,124
- Holy shit.
- Ooh.

240
00:23:30,833 --> 00:23:32,166
- Whoa.
- Previous owner?

241
00:23:32,666 --> 00:23:33,624
Um...

242
00:23:35,249 --> 00:23:36,416
So now what?

243
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,373
Well, he didn't attack you.

244
00:23:39,374 --> 00:23:42,457
He just bolted for the door
unless there's something else.

245
00:23:42,458 --> 00:23:44,833
He's most likely just a squatter.

246
00:23:45,458 --> 00:23:46,998
Left something here.

247
00:23:46,999 --> 00:23:49,290
Didn't realize the place was rented.

248
00:23:49,291 --> 00:23:51,332
Change the locks,
set up a security system,

249
00:23:51,333 --> 00:23:53,416
and donate this stuff to the Goodwill.

250
00:23:53,916 --> 00:23:55,958
And don't forget to bolt your back door.

251
00:23:58,291 --> 00:23:59,374
So that's it?

252
00:23:59,874 --> 00:24:02,749
Fresh coat of paint
on the outside might help ward people off.

253
00:24:53,666 --> 00:24:56,415
<i>If you're lonely, sad, and blue</i>

254
00:24:56,416 --> 00:24:58,749
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

255
00:25:05,041 --> 00:25:07,165
<i>If your window's left unlatched</i>

256
