766
01:03:03,166 --> 01:03:04,623
I know. I know. I know.

767
01:03:04,624 --> 01:03:06,790
It's unbearable, I know.

768
01:03:06,791 --> 01:03:10,457
Jake's gonna come home,
but it has to be to a safe home.

769
01:03:10,458 --> 01:03:13,166
And his dad has to be all right.

770
01:03:13,833 --> 01:03:15,458
I was drinking the night...

771
01:03:16,499 --> 01:03:17,498
We had an argument.

772
01:03:17,499 --> 01:03:20,249
"We had an argument."
I fucking yelled at him.

773
01:03:20,958 --> 01:03:26,791
To walk out that door into the dark,
he had to feel so alone.

774
01:03:30,166 --> 01:03:33,665
When Rebecca died,
he found her at the bottom of the stairs,

775
01:03:33,666 --> 01:03:36,374
and now he can't even
climb a fucking flight of stairs.

776
01:03:38,458 --> 01:03:41,499
I mean, I thought it would be
a good change moving here.

777
01:03:42,583 --> 01:03:44,249
He held on to his mom's stuff.

778
01:03:46,541 --> 01:03:49,916
Photos and notes and old diaries and...

779
01:03:51,874 --> 01:03:53,665
In this satchel.

780
01:03:53,666 --> 01:03:56,833
He called it his Packet of Special Things.

781
01:03:59,041 --> 01:04:00,624
Hey, when you left us,

782
01:04:01,833 --> 01:04:03,832
didn't you want to reach out?

783
01:04:03,833 --> 01:04:06,207
Of course I... I... I...

784
01:04:06,208 --> 01:04:07,208
Every day.

785
01:04:07,958 --> 01:04:10,666
Why didn't you? Weren't you curious?

786
01:04:14,166 --> 01:04:17,665
You know, she never spoke badly
about you, not once, Mom.

787
01:04:17,666 --> 01:04:19,249
Even after everything.

788
01:04:24,124 --> 01:04:27,207
There were times before you guys
moved away where your mother would say,

789
01:04:27,208 --> 01:04:30,916
"Look, you can see him,
but you can't be drinking."

790
01:04:31,749 --> 01:04:35,040
And so I would see you,
and I'd read you stories

791
01:04:35,041 --> 01:04:37,082
when you were about to go to sleep.

792
01:04:37,083 --> 01:04:40,416
And I would tell you how much I love you,
kiss you on the forehead.

793
01:04:41,708 --> 01:04:43,083
And she gave me that.

794
01:04:48,291 --> 01:04:49,624
Mr. Night?

795
01:04:51,124 --> 01:04:52,458
You're Mr. Night?

796
01:04:55,999 --> 01:04:56,958
You?

797
01:04:57,916 --> 01:04:59,333
That was you?

798
01:05:09,374 --> 01:05:11,374
There's an extra bed if you wanna stay.

799
01:05:12,666 --> 01:05:13,708
It's all made up.

800
01:06:49,249 --> 01:06:50,998
They were pen pals.

801
01:06:50,999 --> 01:06:52,416
Did you know about this?

802
01:06:53,666 --> 01:06:56,915
What the fuck else is my dad not sharing?

803
01:06:56,916 --> 01:06:58,458
This isn't the place.

804
01:06:59,041 --> 01:06:59,916
What?

805
01:07:02,624 --> 01:07:05,416
Oh, is... is God listening to us right now?

806
01:07:06,916 --> 01:07:09,374
Maybe that's him, with some leads.

807
01:07:12,208 --> 01:07:14,249
Tell me we have a search warrant.

808
01:08:19,249 --> 01:08:21,416
Where the fuck is this guy going?

809
01:08:48,416 --> 01:08:50,540
Anything else you're not telling us?

810
01:08:50,541 --> 01:08:55,665
Carter sent those letters to hurt my son,
but I kept them secret to deny him that.

811
01:08:55,666 --> 01:08:58,833
You still kept them.
Norman Collins would be impressed.

812
01:09:03,749 --> 01:09:05,708
Fucking prick.

813
01:09:08,041 --> 01:09:09,083
You...

814
01:09:16,291 --> 01:09:18,582
- Where is he?
- What are you doing? My God!

815
01:09:18,583 --> 01:09:20,165
Motherfucker! Where is he?

816
01:09:20,166 --> 01:09:21,498
Where's my boy?

817
01:09:21,499 --> 01:09:22,791
Oh God!

818
01:09:25,374 --> 01:09:27,123
Help! Help!

819
01:09:27,124 --> 01:09:28,290
- Where is he?
- Help!

820
01:09:28,291 --> 01:09:30,583
- Hey! Come on!
- No!

821
01:09:31,249 --> 01:09:34,248
That guy kidnapped my son!
You're letting him get away!

822
01:09:34,249 --> 01:09:37,707
That's the Whisper Man!

823
01:09:37,708 --> 01:09:39,749
Back inside! Let's go! Now!

824
01:09:41,708 --> 01:09:42,707
Back inside!

825
01:09:42,708 --> 01:09:43,957
That's the Whisper Man!

826
01:09:43,958 --> 01:09:47,291
What were you doing
in the basement of 13 Garholt Street?

827
01:09:48,041 --> 01:09:50,498
Uh, I don't know that address.

828
01:09:50,499 --> 01:09:52,623
Norman, stop bullshitting us.

829
01:09:52,624 --> 01:09:54,166
The owner saw you.

830
01:09:55,624 --> 01:09:57,707
If you're referring
to the man who just attacked me,

831
01:09:57,708 --> 01:09:59,290
I've never seen him before in my life.

832
01:09:59,291 --> 01:10:02,999
My guys just searched your place.
This is underlined. So are the others.

833
01:10:05,374 --> 01:10:06,832
I like his stories.

834
01:10:06,833 --> 01:10:08,416
What do you like about them?

835
01:10:08,958 --> 01:10:12,207
Well, he's got this dark mind,

836
01:10:12,208 --> 01:10:13,749
sort of like his daddy's.

837
01:10:14,249 --> 01:10:16,373
We talked to Victor Tyler.

838
01:10:16,374 --> 01:10:20,332
We know that you used him
to pass on a private note to Frank Carter

839
01:10:20,333 --> 01:10:23,623
and a burner phone so he could communicate
with someone on the outside.

840
01:10:23,624 --> 01:10:27,749
And now children are disappearing
and turning up dead.

841
01:10:28,249 --> 01:10:30,123
I don't know, but it all points to you.

842
01:10:30,124 --> 01:10:32,999
- No. No, no, no, no, no.
- Then what?

843
01:10:34,083 --> 01:10:35,999
Were you just getting his autograph?

844
01:10:36,791 --> 01:10:39,374
Another souvenir
for your sicko collection?

845
01:10:42,749 --> 01:10:44,708
I wouldn't hurt those kids, any kids.

846
01:10:46,541 --> 01:10:49,373
- Where the fuck is he going?
- There's not enough to hold him.

847
01:10:49,374 --> 01:10:51,957
He's accounted for both nights
the boys were kidnapped.

848
01:10:51,958 --> 01:10:54,373
In Jake's case,
that man was in another state.

849
01:10:54,374 --> 01:10:56,915
- So he couldn't have taken them.
- Not by himself.

850
01:10:56,916 --> 01:10:59,748
Collins wanted to press assault charges.
Still might.

851
01:10:59,749 --> 01:11:01,248
I hurt him? Are you kidding?

852
01:11:01,249 --> 01:11:03,415
Garretton PD will
only let you walk out of here tonight

853
01:11:03,416 --> 01:11:06,665
if you go home with your father here
and promise not to do anything stupid.

854
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:07,833
This man

855
01:11:08,458 --> 01:11:10,833
knows who has my boy.

856
01:11:17,999 --> 01:11:20,124
Please don't leave me.

857
01:11:27,958 --> 01:11:29,999
I was just trying to protect you.

858
01:11:33,083 --> 01:11:34,458
Yeah, well...

859
01:11:36,624 --> 01:11:41,416
Maybe that's the original sin
of... fathers everywhere.

860
01:11:44,791 --> 01:11:45,833
We can't.

861
01:11:55,958 --> 01:11:57,999
I'll be right back.

862
01:12:42,333 --> 01:12:45,958
What was Norman doing in the basement?

863
01:12:51,958 --> 01:12:54,749
If it really wasn't for Jake,
what was he looking for?

864
01:13:39,333 --> 01:13:40,291
Dad.

865
01:14:43,291 --> 01:14:44,708
Boy in the floor.

866
01:14:54,541 --> 01:14:55,457
<i>Beck here.</i>

867
01:14:55,458 --> 01:14:58,958
Yeah, we're at Garholt Street.
We just found Tony Smith.

868
01:15:17,958 --> 01:15:19,249
Thirty years.

869
01:15:20,624 --> 01:15:21,623
Collins knew.

870
01:15:21,624 --> 01:15:23,958
What are we doing sitting here?

871
01:15:34,208 --> 01:15:36,333
Hey, we got another body over here.

872
01:15:48,124 --> 01:15:50,541
Some kind of blunt instrument.

873
01:15:59,249 --> 01:16:02,040
You better have
a very good excuse for harassing...

874
01:16:02,041 --> 01:16:03,123
Hey! Hey!

875
01:16:03,124 --> 01:16:06,123
We found Tony Smith's remains
on the Garholt property this morning.

876
01:16:06,124 --> 01:16:07,374
And another body.

877
01:16:08,541 --> 01:16:09,582
Provenance.

878
01:16:09,583 --> 01:16:12,666
That's what you collectors call
where a thing comes from, right?

879
01:16:13,874 --> 01:16:15,498
What's the provenance behind this?

880
01:16:15,499 --> 01:16:18,332
Um, that was, uh, acquired off-market.

881
01:16:18,333 --> 01:16:20,208
All aboveboard though, right?

882
01:16:22,791 --> 01:16:24,790
Dominic Barnett. That name ring a bell?

883
01:16:24,791 --> 01:16:27,165
He was found stuffed
in the wall of the basement.

884
01:16:27,166 --> 01:16:28,999
His skull bashed in.

885
01:16:31,208 --> 01:16:33,416
I don't know.
DNA will tell us if it's a match.

886
01:16:38,166 --> 01:16:39,957
Um, I want a lawyer.

887
01:16:39,958 --> 01:16:42,374
You wanted in this game? You're in it.

888
01:16:43,374 --> 01:16:45,374
I didn't hurt any children.

889
01:16:49,541 --> 01:16:50,873
Okay.

890
01:16:50,874 --> 01:16:54,040
I paid Frank Carter for access.

891
01:16:54,041 --> 01:16:57,332
Access? Access to who? Tony Smith?

892
01:16:57,333 --> 01:16:59,957
- Maybe grab something for your collection?
- Okay. Yes.

893
01:16:59,958 --> 01:17:01,790
So he pointed you to Dominic Barnett?

894
01:17:01,791 --> 01:17:05,082
Yeah. Um, they... they were friends
back in the day.

895
01:17:05,083 --> 01:17:07,290
Friends? They weren't friends.
They were accomplices.

896
01:17:07,291 --> 01:17:09,915
What happened between you and Dominic
when you got to the house?

897
01:17:09,916 --> 01:17:11,957
- He, um...
- What happened?

898
01:17:11,958 --> 01:17:14,583
He said, uh... He...

899
01:17:15,999 --> 01:17:16,999
What happened?

900
01:17:17,708 --> 01:17:21,415
In the basement,
he made me feel very small,

901
01:17:21,416 --> 01:17:25,165
saying that I was a tourist
and that I was a Peeping Tom.

902
01:17:25,166 --> 01:17:27,332
That I could jerk off but never fuck.

903
01:17:27,333 --> 01:17:28,373
So you killed him?

904
01:17:28,374 --> 01:17:31,582
You killed him, didn't you?
And that I don't care about.

905
01:17:31,583 --> 01:17:34,041
All I care about is
finding Jake Kennedy alive.

906
01:17:34,916 --> 01:17:36,208
Do you understand?

907
01:17:37,749 --> 01:17:38,749
I can't...

908
01:17:39,249 --> 01:17:40,958
- I can't go to prison.
- You can't?

909
01:17:41,541 --> 01:17:44,041
Well, that's too bad.
You're going to prison.

910
01:17:44,624 --> 01:17:46,040
For a long time.

911
01:17:46,041 --> 01:17:48,624
So you tell us everything
we need to know right now.

912
01:17:49,624 --> 01:17:53,415
You just said you paid Frank Carter
for access to his last victim, Tony Smith,

913
01:17:53,416 --> 01:17:55,915
who was never found.
Is that a fair statement?

914
01:17:55,916 --> 01:17:57,832
- Yes.
- Paid with what?

915
01:17:57,833 --> 01:18:00,833
Carter's in prison for life.
No use for money.

916
01:18:01,333 --> 01:18:03,874
No family anymore. What did you trade?

917
01:18:05,916 --> 01:18:07,748
I connected him with someone.

918
01:18:07,749 --> 01:18:10,541
Who? Norman, who did you connect him to?

919
01:18:11,124 --> 01:18:12,208
Who, Norman?

920
01:18:14,416 --> 01:18:17,583
I was the only one who ever saw it.
In the eyes.

921
01:18:18,083 --> 01:18:20,290
The eyes? Who are you talking about?

922
01:18:20,291 --> 01:18:23,790
I just thought that, you know,
they'd wanna get to know each other.

923
01:18:23,791 --> 01:18:27,248
I never thought that...
that it was gonna start again.

924
01:18:27,249 --> 01:18:30,416
Norman, we need a name. Who is it?

925
01:18:31,499 --> 01:18:34,916
The eyes. Who are you talking about?

926
01:18:46,458 --> 01:18:47,373
We need a bus!

927
01:18:47,374 --> 01:18:50,707
- Help! We need an ambulance!
- Where's Jake? Tell me, where's Jake?

928
01:18:50,708 --> 01:18:53,332
That's the one thing you can do.
Tell me, where's Jake, please?

929
01:18:53,333 --> 01:18:55,623
Where is Jake? Where's Jake?

930
01:18:55,624 --> 01:18:57,998
- Sir!
- Just tell me where he is, please.

931
01:18:57,999 --> 01:18:59,166
Please stand back!

932
01:18:59,874 --> 01:19:01,207
Come on.

933
01:19:01,208 --> 01:19:02,333
Stay with me.

934
01:19:29,791 --> 01:19:33,415
Tom was right. We should have beat
whatever the hell we needed out of him.

935
01:19:33,416 --> 01:19:35,873
Norman said that he thought
Frank Carter would be interested

936
01:19:35,874 --> 01:19:37,915
in getting to know this person. Why?

937
01:19:37,916 --> 01:19:41,165
Why invest in someone
he'll never know, never meet?

938
01:19:41,166 --> 01:19:42,291
Makes no sense.

939
01:19:43,041 --> 01:19:45,624
Who is more important to Frank Carter
than you?

940
01:19:54,166 --> 01:19:57,458
What did Carter say to us
when we were leaving?

941
01:19:57,958 --> 01:19:59,374
The sixth victim?

942
01:20:00,333 --> 01:20:01,208
No.

943
01:20:02,749 --> 01:20:04,708
About my son's novels.

944
01:20:06,583 --> 01:20:08,124
He's trying to be you.

945
01:20:12,374 --> 01:20:14,583
Pull up the interview
with Frank Carter's wife.

946
01:20:19,124 --> 01:20:21,166
That's the one. Play it.

947
01:20:22,874 --> 01:20:24,666
<i>I was afraid for my son.</i>

948
01:20:25,874 --> 01:20:28,748
<i>You don't have
to be afraid anymore, Mrs. Carter.</i>

949
01:20:28,749 --> 01:20:29,958
<i>You're safe now.</i>

950
01:20:31,124 --> 01:20:34,916
<i>There's another boy still missing, though,
and he might still be alive.</i>

951
01:20:35,416 --> 01:20:37,082
<i>You can help us find him.</i>

952
01:20:37,083 --> 01:20:38,749
<i>He's somebody's son too.</i>

953
01:20:39,583 --> 01:20:41,333
<i>I've told you everything I know.</i>

954
01:20:52,916 --> 01:20:55,873
"When we're denied our father's love,

955
01:20:55,874 --> 01:20:57,458
we mythologize him."

956
01:20:59,291 --> 01:21:00,249
It's him.

957
01:21:06,124 --> 01:21:08,958
Do you ever feel like a boy in the floor,

958
01:21:10,583 --> 01:21:12,583
underneath everyone's feet,

959
01:21:13,541 --> 01:21:15,333
who no one knows is there?

960
01:21:16,541 --> 01:21:17,583
I do.

961
01:21:19,166 --> 01:21:22,833
Did the boy in the floor
go to sleep forever?

962
01:21:26,124 --> 01:21:27,208
He did.

963
01:21:32,874 --> 01:21:36,083
Are you going to make me
go to sleep forever?

964
01:21:37,124 --> 01:21:39,124
I'm going to bring you home.

965
01:21:45,208 --> 01:21:48,040
<i>After Carter's conviction,
the family moved out west</i>

966
01:21:48,041 --> 01:21:49,373
and assumed new identities.

967
01:21:49,374 --> 01:21:52,165
We have no name, no ID.

968
01:21:52,166 --> 01:21:55,957
We're negotiating with the FBI
to release whatever records they do have

969
01:21:55,958 --> 01:21:59,165
because, technically, Francis Jr.
is still under their protection.

970
01:21:59,166 --> 01:22:02,832
In the meantime, we need to canvas
anyone and everyone

971
01:22:02,833 --> 01:22:04,998
in Hillcrest
and the surrounding neighborhoods.

972
01:22:04,999 --> 01:22:08,082
If Francis Jr. is here,
someone knows where to find him.

973
01:22:08,083 --> 01:22:09,208
Let's go.

974
01:22:18,999 --> 01:22:20,415
<i>All units be advised.</i>

975
01:22:20,416 --> 01:22:23,290
<i>The suspect has been identified
as Francis Carter, Jr.,</i>

976
01:22:23,291 --> 01:22:25,123
<i>residing in Garretton.</i>

977
01:22:25,124 --> 01:22:29,373
<i>We'll conduct a block-by-block canvas
in an attempt to locate the suspect.</i>

978
01:22:29,374 --> 01:22:30,249
<i>Car 431.</i>

979
01:22:30,958 --> 01:22:33,749
<i>Cover the 400 block of Lafayette,
heading east.</i>

980
01:22:34,333 --> 01:22:38,833
<i>Car 595. Cover Maple Avenue
on the 200 block, heading south.</i>

981
01:23:19,374 --> 01:23:21,166
How's your grandson, Pete?

982
01:23:22,708 --> 01:23:25,582
Good afternoon.
Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

983
01:23:25,583 --> 01:23:27,416
I'm looking for Richard Sharmatz.

984
01:23:28,958 --> 01:23:34,207
Ah, Dr. Sharmatz, uh, passed away
about a year ago.

985
01:23:34,208 --> 01:23:35,707
Oh, his name's still on the title.

986
01:23:35,708 --> 01:23:38,082
His family rents the house to me.

987
01:23:38,083 --> 01:23:40,290
He was a mentor of... of mine.

988
01:23:40,291 --> 01:23:42,373
- Oh.
- I'm George Carringdon.

989
01:23:42,374 --> 01:23:43,290
- Hi.
- Hi.

990
01:23:43,291 --> 01:23:45,249
You a child psychologist as well?

991
01:23:45,749 --> 01:23:47,165
Teaching assistant.

992
01:23:47,166 --> 01:23:48,083
Where?

993
01:23:48,999 --> 01:23:50,166
- Rose Terrace.
- Huh.

994
01:23:50,833 --> 01:23:53,333
Do you know a Jake Kennedy?
He was a student there.

995
01:23:54,958 --> 01:23:57,583
Not until they announced what happened.

996
01:23:58,124 --> 01:24:01,790
I... I probably saw him
running through the halls out at recess,

997
01:24:01,791 --> 01:24:04,707
but, um, I work with
the special needs kids.

998
01:24:04,708 --> 01:24:06,916
- Oh.
- So I wouldn't have known him by name.

999
01:24:08,083 --> 01:24:09,166
Do you want to come in?

1000
01:24:15,624 --> 01:24:18,123
Did you, by any chance,
know the Carter family back in the day?

1001
01:24:18,124 --> 01:24:20,748
Frank and Jane, their son Francis Jr.

1002
01:24:20,749 --> 01:24:21,708
Of them.

1003
01:24:22,208 --> 01:24:26,123
My parents tried to keep me away
from all that stuff. Didn't work.

1004
01:24:26,124 --> 01:24:28,373
We know you've been in communication
with your son,

1005
01:24:28,374 --> 01:24:29,749
prodding him with these killings.

1006
01:24:30,333 --> 01:24:33,790
Boy left home, and now he's back.

1007
01:24:33,791 --> 01:24:34,874
Got lost.

1008
01:24:36,041 --> 01:24:37,291
He's back home now.

1009
01:24:37,791 --> 01:24:38,998
That surprise you?

1010
01:24:38,999 --> 01:24:40,248
Not really, no.

1011
01:24:40,249 --> 01:24:43,999
I mean, Francis has always been weak.
Look how he...

1012
01:24:44,749 --> 01:24:46,666
how he fucked up the first try.

1013
01:24:48,124 --> 01:24:49,873
I guess it's hard with kids.

1014
01:24:49,874 --> 01:24:52,166
Well, scary stories are like water.

1015
01:24:54,666 --> 01:24:56,998
They always find their way
through the cracks.

1016
01:24:56,999 --> 01:25:01,583
I remember growing up in Fair Lawn.
There was this rhyme.

1017
01:25:02,958 --> 01:25:04,832
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

1018
01:25:04,833 --> 01:25:06,873
<i>Soon you'll hear the whisper spoken</i>

1019
01:25:06,874 --> 01:25:09,748
- <i>If your window's...</i>
- <i>...left unlatched</i>

1020
01:25:09,749 --> 01:25:11,624
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

1021
01:25:12,124 --> 01:25:14,541
<i>- If you're lonely...</i>
- <i>...sad, or blue...</i>

1022
01:25:16,541 --> 01:25:18,583
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

1023
01:25:25,416 --> 01:25:27,749
Been a long time
since I've heard that one.

1024
01:25:33,208 --> 01:25:35,166
I was making tea. You want a cup?

1025
01:25:40,541 --> 01:25:42,998
I get now
why you always covered their faces.

1026
01:25:42,999 --> 01:25:46,290
I thought it was 'cause you couldn't look
at 'em or didn't want them looking at you.

1027
01:25:46,291 --> 01:25:48,457
Nah, I could look at their faces
just fine.

1028
01:25:48,458 --> 01:25:49,957
Oh, that's bullshit. Come on.

1029
01:25:49,958 --> 01:25:52,040
You know there was someone
you were imagining

1030
01:25:52,041 --> 01:25:55,124
you wanted to get a hold of
but you couldn't really get your hands on.

1031
01:25:56,874 --> 01:25:58,998
It was too painful, too messy,

1032
01:25:58,999 --> 01:26:00,332
too close to home.

1033
01:26:00,333 --> 01:26:03,499
Well... home is where the heart is, Pete.

1034
01:26:04,666 --> 01:26:09,083
Is there some sort of connection
between Frank Carter and Dr. Sharmatz?

1035
01:26:10,083 --> 01:26:14,124
He counseled Carter's son,
according to records.

1036
01:26:16,583 --> 01:26:18,916
Police must be stretched pretty thin.

1037
01:26:20,166 --> 01:26:22,041
No partner, I see.

1038
01:26:23,624 --> 01:26:25,791
Everybody has their ground to cover.

1039
01:26:26,458 --> 01:26:30,999
I know the parents will be relieved
that you're chasing down some leads.

1040
01:26:31,624 --> 01:26:34,249
Yeah. Kids, too, I'm guessing.

1041
01:26:34,749 --> 01:26:37,583
Francis is learning his own lessons
right now.

1042
01:26:38,083 --> 01:26:40,416
Yeah. Like you did with your father?

1043
01:26:41,958 --> 01:26:43,498
The way he taught you.

1044
01:26:43,499 --> 01:26:45,915
Whispering to you in bed
while he was fucking you up the ass?

1045
01:26:45,916 --> 01:26:47,540
You better shut up.

1046
01:26:47,541 --> 01:26:49,623
How'd you handle those situations, Frank?

1047
01:26:49,624 --> 01:26:52,290
Did you wish you were somewhere
like the kids you took did too?

1048
01:26:52,291 --> 01:26:53,540
- Fuck you.
- Ah.

1049
01:26:53,541 --> 01:26:55,790
Your father whet his appetite
with his own son.

1050
01:26:55,791 --> 01:26:58,249
- Fuck you.
- But you, you were the weak one.

1051
01:27:01,958 --> 01:27:04,498
I actually respect you, Frank.
You know that?

1052
01:27:04,499 --> 01:27:08,374
You tried to stop yourself from doing
what you really wanted to do to your boy.

1053
01:27:08,874 --> 01:27:09,874
Yeah.

1054
01:27:11,041 --> 01:27:12,790
So you preyed on others.

1055
01:27:12,791 --> 01:27:15,665
When we catch your son,
and we're gonna catch him very soon...

1056
01:27:15,666 --> 01:27:18,290
- Yeah?
- You're never gonna hear from him again.

1057
01:27:18,291 --> 01:27:20,582
Oh, really? So...

1058
01:27:20,583 --> 01:27:22,583
So there's another possibility.

1059
01:27:23,749 --> 01:27:24,708
Jake.

1060
01:27:25,499 --> 01:27:26,958
You can tell me where he is.

1061
01:27:30,833 --> 01:27:32,707
Why would I do that before the deed?

1062
01:27:32,708 --> 01:27:35,583
Because the Whisper Man,
the real one, isn't done yet.

1063
01:27:36,166 --> 01:27:39,082
Because there's only one child
in this whole world

1064
01:27:39,083 --> 01:27:41,541
that he truly, really wants.

1065
01:27:42,041 --> 01:27:43,833
And I can deliver him to you.

1066
01:27:45,333 --> 01:27:46,583
My son?

1067
01:27:51,333 --> 01:27:52,373
Here?

1068
01:27:52,374 --> 01:27:55,541
A father does what needs to be done.
Wouldn't you agree?

1069
01:27:59,916 --> 01:28:02,457
If you think of anyone
that might know the Carter family,

1070
01:28:02,458 --> 01:28:06,166
especially Francis Jr.,
please have them call me, okay?

1071
01:28:09,666 --> 01:28:11,249
Of course.

1072
01:28:20,791 --> 01:28:22,583
Oh fuck!

1073
01:28:30,624 --> 01:28:34,623
This is Beck. I need backup.
59 Hellerman Street. I found our suspect.

1074
01:28:34,624 --> 01:28:36,458
<i>Copy that.</i>

1075
01:28:37,041 --> 01:28:38,374
Jake Kennedy?

1076
01:28:39,249 --> 01:28:40,583
This is the police.

1077
01:30:26,416 --> 01:30:27,749
Scream.

1078
01:30:31,583 --> 01:30:34,291
Help!

1079
01:30:57,041 --> 01:30:59,499
Get up! Come on!

1080
01:31:21,416 --> 01:31:23,166
Run!

1081
01:31:25,874 --> 01:31:26,833
Run!

1082
01:31:38,791 --> 01:31:40,207
Help!

1083
01:31:40,208 --> 01:31:41,249
Stop!

1084
01:31:42,291 --> 01:31:44,958
Help! Help!

1085
01:32:15,541 --> 01:32:17,415
<i>Detective Beck. Leave a message.</i>

1086
01:32:17,416 --> 01:32:19,916
Beck. Yeah. It's me.

1087
01:32:20,666 --> 01:32:23,166
I spoke to Carter.
They have a plan for Jake.

1088
01:32:39,124 --> 01:32:41,332
<i>Garretton Police. What's your emergency?</i>

1089
01:32:41,333 --> 01:32:43,457
I just saw the missing boy, Jake Kennedy.

1090
01:32:43,458 --> 01:32:46,248
He was with a man,
Route 23, south of Sussex.

1091
01:32:46,249 --> 01:32:48,748
<i>Dispatch 10-17. We have units en route.</i>

1092
01:32:48,749 --> 01:32:51,416
<i>Can I please have your name
and a callback number?</i>

1093
01:33:20,166 --> 01:33:22,541
What the hell?

1094
01:33:27,291 --> 01:33:29,708
Come on, Tom. Please pick up.

1095
01:33:41,541 --> 01:33:42,416
<i>Dad?</i>

1096
01:33:50,499 --> 01:33:51,666
Sh.

1097
01:35:11,791 --> 01:35:13,582
- I can't breathe!
- Jake!

1098
01:35:13,583 --> 01:35:14,624
Dad, help!

1099
01:35:30,166 --> 01:35:31,874
Help!

1100
01:35:40,333 --> 01:35:42,916
Jake!

1101
01:35:52,708 --> 01:35:54,333
Oh, Jake. It's okay.

1102
01:35:58,749 --> 01:36:00,499
Come on. Come on. Go.

1103
01:36:12,624 --> 01:36:14,166
Dad!

1104
01:36:19,583 --> 01:36:20,541
Dad!

1105
01:36:21,374 --> 01:36:23,333
No!

1106
01:36:25,833 --> 01:36:29,416
Dad!

1107
01:36:30,041 --> 01:36:31,040
Jake!

1108
01:36:31,041 --> 01:36:32,333
- Dad!
- Jake!

1109
01:36:34,291 --> 01:36:36,374
Run! Run, Jake!

1110
01:36:36,874 --> 01:36:37,708
Run!

1111
01:36:49,958 --> 01:36:52,332
Tommy, Tommy. Get Jake.

1112
01:36:52,333 --> 01:36:54,373
- Go get Jake.
- Dad! What?

1113
01:36:54,374 --> 01:36:56,249
- I love you.
- I love you.

1114
01:37:50,374 --> 01:37:51,916
Daddy!

1115
01:37:53,041 --> 01:37:54,583
Daddy!

1116
01:38:04,041 --> 01:38:05,083
Jake.

1117
01:38:06,083 --> 01:38:09,208
Just stay. Stay there.

1118
01:38:10,333 --> 01:38:13,416
Jake, close your eyes.

1119
01:38:16,041 --> 01:38:17,333
Agh!

1120
01:40:16,124 --> 01:40:17,958
Just make it quick, Carter.

1121
01:40:33,166 --> 01:40:34,749
Skin to skin,

1122
01:40:36,791 --> 01:40:38,749
like they said in the hospital,

1123
01:40:39,624 --> 01:40:41,666
to bond you to me.

1124
01:42:08,499 --> 01:42:11,123
What's Pearl Jam?

1125
01:42:11,124 --> 01:42:13,123
What? A band!

1126
01:42:13,124 --> 01:42:14,832
Clearly failed as a father.

1127
01:42:14,833 --> 01:42:16,958
It was our first concert, your mom and me.

1128
01:42:20,666 --> 01:42:21,666
She saved me.

1129
01:42:30,041 --> 01:42:31,041
Mommy?

1130
01:42:31,541 --> 01:42:32,458
Mm-hmm.

1131
01:42:35,166 --> 01:42:36,374
Yeah, me too.

1132
01:42:40,624 --> 01:42:42,291
Can I go play?

1133
01:42:43,999 --> 01:42:44,958
Yeah, dude.

1134
01:42:46,916 --> 01:42:48,082
Get out there.

1135
01:42:48,083 --> 01:42:49,666
What are you doing in here?

1136
01:42:56,874 --> 01:42:58,041
Hey, guys!




